Source: audioledd
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tommie Gannert <tommie.gh@gannert.se>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: audioledd
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0 (>= 2.80), pulseaudio-utils (>= 16), systemd
Description: mute LEDs following the default audio devices
 The kernel only lights the speaker and mic mute LEDs for ALSA sound cards.
 This daemon makes them follow the default sink and source of the active
 seat session instead, so muting e.g. a Bluetooth headset lights them too.
 When the default device is the built-in card, the kernel stays in control.
